{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1myaUdxMMGxWk7NRhQ2", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with a PASS at 0.6 confidence. I filed no confirmed bugs. I reported one Cloze menu difference, but the developer could not reproduce it, so I left it out of the findings.\n\n**What I checked**\n- **Add-note card preview:** Basic, \"Basic (and reversed card)\", Cloze, and \"Basic (optional reversed card)\" all showed the right page for each card tab. That includes the reverse card, both Cloze cards, and the \"The front of this card is blank.\" page for an empty conditional card. Filling in that card's field updated its page.\n- **Template editor menu:** Basic, \"Basic (and reversed card)\" and Cloze each showed a menu that fits its template count. The Cloze menu lacks \"Rename card type\" and \"Deck override\", which Basic has. The developer could not reproduce that, so I dropped it.\n- **Deck list:** I created a temporary parent deck with one child to get an expand arrow. Expanding and collapsing worked, the rows below kept the right counts, the expanded state survived a rotation, and I deleted the temporary decks afterwards.\n- **Note types:** the counts matched the data. Basic showed 8 notes after my test note, and the other types showed 0.\n\n**Side effect to know about:** by mis-tapping during Add note, I saved a Basic note with Front \"cat\" and an empty Back. It is still in the Default deck and I did not remove it.\n\n**Not covered:** child decks holding cards, Image Occlusion preview, and multi-template types with three or more templates (none exist in this build)."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1114, "cache_read_input_tokens": 155997, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1114}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier